[{"text": "The assembly will hear an address by his", "start": 0.719, "duration": 6.321}, {"text": "excellency Tarik Rahman, Prime Minister", "start": 3.84, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "of the Government of People's Republic", "start": 7.04, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "of Bangladesh.", "start": 8.96, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "I request protocol to escort his", "start": 11.84, "duration": 5.439}, {"text": "excellency Tariq Raman and invite him to", "start": 14.4, "duration": 6.44}, {"text": "address the assembly.", "start": 17.279, "duration": 3.561}, {"text": ">> [clears throat]", "start": 32.75, "duration": 2.02}, {"text": ">> Rahman Rahim.", "start": 43.44, "duration": 5.4}, {"text": "Mr. President,", "start": 45.44, "duration": 3.4}, {"text": "I congratulate you on your election as", "start": 49.36, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "President of the 81st session of the", "start": 53.12, "duration": 6.36}, {"text": "United Nations General Assembly.", "start": 55.28, "duration": 4.2}, {"text": "I assure you of our full support and", "start": 61.68, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "cooperation as you discharge your", "start": 64.72, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "responsibilities as president.", "start": 66.72, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "At the same time, I extend my gratitude", "start": 69.6, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "to the outgoing president, Madame", "start": 73.28, "duration": 7.519}, {"text": "Analena Berbach for her able leadership.", "start": 75.68, "duration": 7.36}, {"text": "Let me begin by paying my deepest", "start": 80.799, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "respect to all the martyrd freedom", "start": 83.04, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "fighters of Bangladesh.", "start": 85.759, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "I respectfully remember the", "start": 88.56, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "contributions of those who have made the", "start": 91.36, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "ultimate sacrifice in the struggle to", "start": 94.32, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "establish democracy, justice and", "start": 97.2, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "people's rights in our country since", "start": 99.6, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "independence.", "start": 102.32, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "I also pay my sincere respect to all", "start": 104.4, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "those who were martyed and injured in", "start": 107.6, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "the mass uprising of courageous students", "start": 110.32, "duration": 6.079}, {"text": "and people in July August 2024 against", "start": 113.119, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "fascism.", "start": 116.399, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "After more than a decade and a half of", "start": 118.079, "duration": 5.441}, {"text": "movement and struggle against fascist", "start": 121.439, "duration": 4.561}, {"text": "rule and exploitation and through the", "start": 123.52, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "sacrifice of thousands of lives,", "start": 126.0, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "Bangladesh is now free from fascism. In", "start": 128.479, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "a free, fair and impartial national", "start": 132.08, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "election held on 12th February this", "start": 134.959, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "year. The people entrusted the", "start": 137.76, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "Bangladesh Nationalist Party BNP with", "start": 139.76, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "the responsibility of governing the", "start": 142.72, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "country. I congratulate the democracy", "start": 144.64, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "loving people of Bangladesh.", "start": 147.76, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "We believe that the people are the", "start": 151.36, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "source of all our political power.", "start": 153.36, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "Standing on this world stage of the", "start": 156.959, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "United Nations, I am somewhat nostalgic", "start": 159.28, "duration": 6.84}, {"text": "at this moment.", "start": 162.64, "duration": 3.48}, {"text": "It was from this very world stage that", "start": 166.16, "duration": 9.079}, {"text": "my father Shahit President Zor Rahman", "start": 169.68, "duration": 5.559}, {"text": "The proclaimer of Bangladesh's", "start": 175.92, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "independence and my mother, former prime", "start": 177.68, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "minister Le Beam Khaledia address the", "start": 180.959, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "world on behalf of the country and its", "start": 183.44, "duration": 4.719}, {"text": "people.", "start": 185.76, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "Today I too", "start": 188.159, "duration": 5.841}, {"text": "stand here to speak for the interests of", "start": 191.68, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "my country", "start": 194.0, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "and its people and in the hope of a", "start": 196.4, "duration": 7.0}, {"text": "peaceful world community.", "start": 199.519, "duration": 3.881}, {"text": "In this age of globalization,", "start": 204.879, "duration": 6.481}, {"text": "whatever happens in any part of the", "start": 208.48, "duration": 6.479}, {"text": "world has to varying degrees a negative", "start": 211.36, "duration": 7.519}, {"text": "impact on every country.", "start": 214.959, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "Human-made conflicts have created", "start": 218.879, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "situations of unrest in many countries.", "start": 220.959, "duration": 6.081}, {"text": "Vast numbers of people are being", "start": 224.56, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "displaced giving rise to humanitarian", "start": 227.04, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "crisis.", "start": 230.08, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "Wars and conflicts are placing immense", "start": 232.48, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "pressure on the global economy.", "start": 235.44, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "Energy security concerns,", "start": 238.64, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "disruptions to global energy supply", "start": 241.2, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "systems and rising inflation are", "start": 243.28, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "worsening the economic situation.", "start": 245.84, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "We believe that every conflict should be", "start": 249.36, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "resolved through dialogue, diplomatic", "start": 252.0, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "processes and mutual cooperation.", "start": 254.56, "duration": 7.44}, {"text": "Equality, fairness, protection of mutual", "start": 258.72, "duration": 6.479}, {"text": "interests and respect and dignity among", "start": 262.0, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "disputing states should form the basis", "start": 265.199, "duration": 8.161}, {"text": "of bilateral and multilateral relations.", "start": 268.4, "duration": 8.72}, {"text": "We aspire to a peaceful world, a humane", "start": 273.36, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "global community where rather than", "start": 277.12, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "weapons of destruction, reason and", "start": 280.0, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "debate, diplomacy, education and", "start": 283.12, "duration": 6.079}, {"text": "humanity become the instruments of", "start": 286.4, "duration": 5.799}, {"text": "change.", "start": 289.199, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "Bangladesh sees the United Nations as", "start": 293.12, "duration": 7.04}, {"text": "the centerpiece for establishing an", "start": 296.56, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "accommodative global community based on", "start": 300.16, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "mutual respect for one another's", "start": 302.96, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "independence and sovereignity.", "start": 305.199, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "The tendency to divert development", "start": 309.28, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "budgets towards military expenditure in", "start": 311.759, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "different parts of the world re reverses", "start": 314.72, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "the direction of our journey towards", "start": 317.44, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "global peace. As a peace-loving nation,", "start": 319.36, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "Bangladesh remains committed to the", "start": 322.88, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "goals of complete and general", "start": 324.72, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "disarmament, preventing the", "start": 326.56, "duration": 4.079}, {"text": "proliferation of nuclear weapons and", "start": 328.56, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "arms control.", "start": 330.639, "duration": 6.241}, {"text": "I reiterate Bangladesh's support for any", "start": 333.919, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "initiative at the United Nations", "start": 336.88, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "dedicated to establishing world peace", "start": 339.52, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "and serving humanity.", "start": 342.0, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "The people of Bangladesh who believe in", "start": 345.039, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "democracy remain deeply concerned about", "start": 347.68, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "the plight of the freedomseeking", "start": 350.96, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "Palestinian people.", "start": 352.8, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "Bangladesh once again reaffirms its", "start": 355.6, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "unwavering support for their legitimate", "start": 358.4, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "demands including their right to", "start": 360.96, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "self-determination and their right to", "start": 363.12, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "establish an independent state of", "start": 365.12, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "Palestine. Mr. President in the", "start": 367.12, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "prevailing global circumstances the", "start": 369.919, "duration": 4.321}, {"text": "theme of the 81st session of the United", "start": 372.08, "duration": 5.119}, {"text": "Nations General Assembly restoring trust", "start": 374.24, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "managing transformation a United Nations", "start": 377.199, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "that delivers for all is highly relevant", "start": 380.0, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "and timely. Bangladesh remains steadfast", "start": 382.4, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "in its commitment to multilateralism in", "start": 385.84, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "maintaining international peace and", "start": 388.24, "duration": 4.079}, {"text": "security. As vice chair of the", "start": 390.08, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "peaceuilding commission, Bangladesh", "start": 392.319, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "continues to serve as a strong voice for", "start": 394.72, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "sustainable peace, conflict prevention", "start": 397.12, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "and inclusive peace.", "start": 399.759, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "As a consistent contributor to United", "start": 402.16, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "Nations peacekeeping missions,", "start": 404.72, "duration": 4.319}, {"text": "Bangladeshi peacekeepers are serving", "start": 406.8, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "humanity in different parts of the", "start": 409.039, "duration": 5.841}, {"text": "world. The courageous participation of", "start": 411.44, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "Bangladeshi women in peacekeeping", "start": 414.88, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "missions even under adverse", "start": 417.28, "duration": 3.52}, {"text": "circumstances", "start": 419.28, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "reflects our strong commitment to", "start": 420.8, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "advancing the agenda of women peace and", "start": 422.96, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "security.", "start": 425.599, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "This year Bangladesh is observing the", "start": 428.08, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "40th anniversary of the declaration on", "start": 430.639, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "the right to development and the 25th", "start": 433.68, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "anniversary of the Darban declaration", "start": 435.919, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "and program of action. Migration is as", "start": 438.479, "duration": 6.801}, {"text": "old as human civilization. In many", "start": 442.319, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "countries around the world, migrants", "start": 445.28, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "make important contributions to the", "start": 447.919, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "economies of both their countries of", "start": 449.84, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "origin and their countries of", "start": 451.919, "duration": 4.161}, {"text": "destination. The government of", "start": 454.16, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "Bangladesh is committed to ensuring", "start": 456.08, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "regular, safe and orderly migration.", "start": 458.08, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "Bangladesh expects stronger global", "start": 461.84, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "cooperation to ensure the rights,", "start": 464.08, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "dignity and well-being of migrants. Mr.", "start": 466.08, "duration": 7.6}, {"text": "president. For more than 9 years,", "start": 469.759, "duration": 6.641}, {"text": "Bangladesh has been sheltering more than", "start": 473.68, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "1.2 million forcibly displaced Rohhinga", "start": 476.4, "duration": 4.639}, {"text": "from Myanmar.", "start": 479.28, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "This has placed immense pressure on our", "start": 481.039, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "resources, environment, security and", "start": 483.84, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "local communities. As a densely", "start": 486.639, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "populated country, Bangladesh believes", "start": 489.12, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "that the source and origin of the", "start": 492.0, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "Rohhinga crisis lie in Myanmar.", "start": 493.919, "duration": 7.68}, {"text": "Therefore, its solution also lies there.", "start": 496.8, "duration": 8.079}, {"text": "The only solution to this problem is the", "start": 501.599, "duration": 5.121}, {"text": "early safe return of the displaced", "start": 504.879, "duration": 3.681}, {"text": "Rohhinga people to their homeland", "start": 506.72, "duration": 4.159}, {"text": "Myanmar.", "start": 508.56, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "For a lasting solution to this crisis,", "start": 510.879, "duration": 5.761}, {"text": "Bangladesh expects firm and effective", "start": 514.24, "duration": 4.719}, {"text": "support from the United Nations and the", "start": 516.64, "duration": 4.879}, {"text": "international community.", "start": 518.959, "duration": 5.281}, {"text": "At the same time, I call upon the United", "start": 521.519, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "Nations and the international community", "start": 524.24, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "to continue life-saving assistance", "start": 526.56, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "programs for the displaced Rohingya", "start": 529.279, "duration": 5.761}, {"text": "people until they can be repatriated to", "start": 532.0, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "their own country, Myanmar.", "start": 535.04, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "If the international community fails to", "start": 538.56, "duration": 5.279}, {"text": "ensure justice for the displaced", "start": 541.44, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "Rohhinga people, this could turn into a", "start": 543.839, "duration": 6.081}, {"text": "humanitarian crisis in the near future.", "start": 546.8, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "Mr. President", "start": 549.92, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "Bangladesh", "start": 552.72, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "is one of the countries most vulnerable", "start": 554.24, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "to the adverse impacts of climate", "start": 557.12, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "change.", "start": 559.2, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "Although Bangladesh has contributed", "start": 561.2, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "little to global carbon emissions, it is", "start": 563.12, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "bearing the adverse consequences of", "start": 566.16, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "climate change.", "start": 568.32, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "In these circumstances, Bangladesh has", "start": 570.48, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "chosen the path of building resilience", "start": 573.12, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "and developing the capacity to survive", "start": 575.68, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "and adapt. Therefore, Bangladesh expects", "start": 578.0, "duration": 7.92}, {"text": "stronger global cooperation at COP 31 on", "start": 581.92, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "climate justice, climate finance and", "start": 585.92, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "adaptation support.", "start": 588.24, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "The government of Bangladesh has", "start": 591.12, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "strengthened its programs for", "start": 593.279, "duration": 4.401}, {"text": "environmental protection.", "start": 595.12, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "As part of these efforts, the government", "start": 597.68, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "has launched a program to plant 250", "start": 600.48, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "million trees across the country over", "start": 603.6, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "the next 5 years. Emphasis has been", "start": 605.6, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "placed on the use of clean energy and", "start": 608.8, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "solar energy", "start": 611.04, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "with the aim of freeing the country from", "start": 613.12, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "the scourge of floods and droughts. The", "start": 615.6, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "government has also launched a program", "start": 618.56, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "to excavate", "start": 620.56, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "20,000 kilometers of canel across the", "start": 622.48, "duration": 8.64}, {"text": "country. The government has also began", "start": 626.24, "duration": 8.08}, {"text": "work on the Thista master plan and the", "start": 631.12, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "Poda barage project to increase", "start": 634.32, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "freshwater flows into the world's", "start": 636.88, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "largest mangro forest, the Sundurbans,", "start": 638.72, "duration": 4.559}, {"text": "and to conserve water through large", "start": 641.2, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "reservoirs. At the same time, while", "start": 643.279, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "strengthening domestic measures for", "start": 646.24, "duration": 3.599}, {"text": "water conservation and pollution", "start": 648.079, "duration": 4.481}, {"text": "prevention, the government has", "start": 649.839, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "reaffirmed its commitment to cooperation", "start": 652.56, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "on transboundary water management by", "start": 654.64, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "signing the 1992 water convention. Mr.", "start": 657.44, "duration": 6.8}, {"text": "President, after ending more than a", "start": 661.04, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "decade and a half of fascist rule and", "start": 664.24, "duration": 4.719}, {"text": "exploitation, Bangladesh became free", "start": 666.32, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "from fascism in 2024.", "start": 668.959, "duration": 5.281}, {"text": "Having been freed from the scourges of", "start": 671.68, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "enforced disappearances, killings,", "start": 674.24, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "abductions, corruption, plunder, and", "start": 676.48, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "money laundering that had become the", "start": 679.04, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "norm under fascist rule. Bangladesh is", "start": 681.279, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "now once again embarking on the path of", "start": 684.56, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "democracy. To repair a Bangladesh", "start": 686.88, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "battered by fascist rule and", "start": 690.079, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "exploitation, the government is pursuing", "start": 691.76, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "a three-R strategy: recovery,", "start": 694.399, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "restoration, and reconstruction.", "start": 696.72, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "A vast horizon of opportunities has now", "start": 700.32, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "opened before Bangladesh.", "start": 703.12, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "Taking advantage of the demographic", "start": 705.36, "duration": 4.479}, {"text": "dividend, the government has begun", "start": 707.2, "duration": 5.199}, {"text": "implementing extensive programs to", "start": 709.839, "duration": 4.481}, {"text": "transform the country's working age", "start": 712.399, "duration": 4.401}, {"text": "population into a skilled human", "start": 714.32, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "resource. The government has also", "start": 716.8, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "undertaken some forward-looking", "start": 719.36, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "initiatives to create large-scale", "start": 721.2, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "employment opportunities and transform", "start": 723.68, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "Bangladesh into a manufacturing hub. In", "start": 726.32, "duration": 6.319}, {"text": "this endeavor, Bangladesh wants its", "start": 729.36, "duration": 7.12}, {"text": "development partners by its side to to", "start": 732.639, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "create opportunities for young", "start": 736.48, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "entrepreneurs,", "start": 738.24, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "researchers and innovators in the", "start": 740.48, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "country to pursue startup initiatives.", "start": 743.04, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "The government has allocated $50 million", "start": 745.6, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "US in the current fiscal year.", "start": 748.32, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "Mr. President,", "start": 751.92, "duration": 3.599}, {"text": "more than half of the country's", "start": 753.92, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "population is female. Therefore, women", "start": 755.519, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "are at the forefront of all government", "start": 759.12, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "plans for socioeconomic transformation.", "start": 761.2, "duration": 6.319}, {"text": "The government is giving priority to", "start": 764.8, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "women's education, women's employment", "start": 767.519, "duration": 6.241}, {"text": "and the creation of women entrepreneurs.", "start": 769.92, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "To promote women entrepreneurship,", "start": 773.76, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "particularly in the small and", "start": 776.16, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "medium-sized industrial sector, the", "start": 777.92, "duration": 4.719}, {"text": "government has expanded opportunities", "start": 780.56, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "for cash financing for women.", "start": 782.639, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "Free education opportunities up to the", "start": 786.24, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "undergraduate level have been opened to", "start": 788.56, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "women. The government seeks to ensure", "start": 791.12, "duration": 7.44}, {"text": "not only electoral democracy but also", "start": 795.12, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "democratization of the economy so that", "start": 798.56, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "the benefits of economic growth and", "start": 801.36, "duration": 4.719}, {"text": "prosperity reach every family and every", "start": 803.44, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "citizen. To achieve this goal, the", "start": 806.079, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "government has already launched", "start": 809.12, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "assistance programs for economically", "start": 810.959, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "disadvantaged people through various", "start": 813.68, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "social protection programs including the", "start": 816.16, "duration": 5.919}, {"text": "family card, farmers card, sports card,", "start": 819.04, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "and e- health card.", "start": 822.079, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "The government considers the family card", "start": 825.36, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "issued in the name of the female head of", "start": 828.0, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "each household a symbol of women's", "start": 830.56, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "economic empowerment.", "start": 833.2, "duration": 5.439}, {"text": "It is also in the government's plans to", "start": 836.079, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "introduce a universal card by", "start": 838.639, "duration": 5.121}, {"text": "integrating the various card introduced", "start": 841.44, "duration": 6.88}, {"text": "to provide support in different sectors.", "start": 843.76, "duration": 6.96}, {"text": "Mr. President,", "start": 848.32, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "the government is implementing", "start": 850.72, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "the 31point", "start": 853.76, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "program presented to the people before", "start": 855.76, "duration": 5.759}, {"text": "the national election of 12th February", "start": 858.48, "duration": 6.039}, {"text": "2026.", "start": 861.519, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "At least", "start": 864.959, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "73% of the activities under the", "start": 866.639, "duration": 6.241}, {"text": "government's 31point program have a", "start": 869.279, "duration": 7.92}, {"text": "direct alignment and 27% an indirect", "start": 872.88, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "alignment with the United Nations", "start": 877.199, "duration": 4.561}, {"text": "sustainable development goals and their", "start": 879.36, "duration": 4.479}, {"text": "guiding principle of leave no one", "start": 881.76, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "behind. The government hopes that", "start": 883.839, "duration": 4.321}, {"text": "through the implementation of these", "start": 886.48, "duration": 4.159}, {"text": "programs, development disparities", "start": 888.16, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "between urban and rural areas will be", "start": 890.639, "duration": 5.121}, {"text": "reduced while accountability and", "start": 893.04, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "inclusive sustainable development will", "start": 895.76, "duration": 6.079}, {"text": "be advanced across all areas of the 2030", "start": 898.24, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "agenda.", "start": 901.839, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "The government of Bangladesh has", "start": 903.68, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "accorded special importance to", "start": 905.519, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "education, health and sports. The", "start": 907.92, "duration": 5.279}, {"text": "highest budgetary allocation in the", "start": 910.88, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "country's history have been made in the", "start": 913.199, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "education sector. Our plan is to", "start": 915.92, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "increase budgetary allocation to", "start": 919.12, "duration": 6.159}, {"text": "education to 5% of GDP within next 5", "start": 921.6, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "years.", "start": 925.279, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "A curriculum has been developed with", "start": 927.92, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "emphasis on tech technical and practical", "start": 930.88, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "education to ensure an employment", "start": 933.68, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "oriented education system with strong", "start": 936.56, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "ethical values. From the first grade,", "start": 939.199, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "primary school students are being", "start": 942.8, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "provided with school bags and clothing", "start": 944.72, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "that is school uniforms as well as free", "start": 947.199, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "lunch. The government hopes that this", "start": 950.0, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "will increase school enrollment and", "start": 952.88, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "improve the quality of education", "start": 955.04, "duration": 7.039}, {"text": "to establish sports as a profession.", "start": 958.16, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "Sports has been included as a subject in", "start": 962.079, "duration": 4.241}, {"text": "the education curriculum for the first", "start": 964.32, "duration": 3.759}, {"text": "time.", "start": 966.32, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "As part of this initiative, more than 2", "start": 968.079, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "million students", "start": 971.04, "duration": 6.479}, {"text": "participated in a month-long nationwide", "start": 972.959, "duration": 7.201}, {"text": "football tournament for school students", "start": 977.519, "duration": 7.801}, {"text": "held last June. Mr. President,", "start": 980.16, "duration": 5.16}, {"text": "science and technology will shape the", "start": 986.72, "duration": 5.96}, {"text": "future of the world.", "start": 988.959, "duration": 3.721}, {"text": "We are entering a new era of artificial", "start": 993.04, "duration": 6.159}, {"text": "intelligence, biotechnology and science.", "start": 995.68, "duration": 6.399}, {"text": "Technology is advancing very rapidly,", "start": 999.199, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "but its opportunities are still not", "start": 1002.079, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "equally accessible to all. Bangladesh's", "start": 1004.16, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "large young population and growing", "start": 1007.519, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "digital capabilities have created new", "start": 1009.68, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "possibilities for us", "start": 1012.72, "duration": 5.919}, {"text": "to harness these opportunities. Access", "start": 1016.32, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "to advanced technology, knowledge and", "start": 1018.639, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "research must be brought within", "start": 1021.36, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "everyone's reach.", "start": 1023.44, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "We do not want today's digital divide to", "start": 1025.6, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "become tomorrow's artificial", "start": 1028.0, "duration": 3.839}, {"text": "intelligence divide.", "start": 1029.6, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "Bangladesh respects innovation and", "start": 1031.839, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "intellectual property. At the same time,", "start": 1034.4, "duration": 5.919}, {"text": "it is essential to ensure technology", "start": 1037.439, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "transfer, skills development and", "start": 1040.319, "duration": 4.561}, {"text": "affordable access to modern technologies", "start": 1042.48, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "for developing countries.", "start": 1044.88, "duration": 6.159}, {"text": "No country should be left behind in this", "start": 1048.079, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "scientific advancement.", "start": 1051.039, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "Bangladesh stands ready to work together", "start": 1053.28, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "to build a fair and prosperous future", "start": 1055.919, "duration": 5.841}, {"text": "for all. It is now time for the United", "start": 1058.32, "duration": 7.2}, {"text": "Nations to adopt an effective policy", "start": 1061.76, "duration": 6.159}, {"text": "framework so that the benefits of the", "start": 1065.52, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "development and rapid expansion of", "start": 1067.919, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "artificial intelligence and social media", "start": 1069.919, "duration": 4.721}, {"text": "can be harnessed positively across", "start": 1072.72, "duration": 7.64}, {"text": "countries. Mr. President Bangladesh.", "start": 1074.64, "duration": 5.72}, {"text": ">> Bangladesh is awaiting graduation from", "start": 1080.559, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "the list of least developed countries.", "start": 1082.96, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "For Bangladesh as well as for all other", "start": 1086.16, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "countries undergoing this process,", "start": 1088.96, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "sustained support in areas such as", "start": 1091.6, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "assured financing, greater market", "start": 1094.08, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "access, technology transfer and capacity", "start": 1096.72, "duration": 5.839}, {"text": "building is essential to make the", "start": 1100.32, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "graduation process sustainable.", "start": 1102.559, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "In the present world order, all", "start": 1105.679, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "countries are interdependent.", "start": 1108.24, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "Bangladesh believes that particularly at", "start": 1111.28, "duration": 5.759}, {"text": "the regional level,", "start": 1114.4, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "we can help one another achieve", "start": 1117.039, "duration": 6.161}, {"text": "prosperity through the facilitation and", "start": 1120.32, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "expansion of trade, effective", "start": 1123.2, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "connectivity and meaningful cooperation.", "start": 1124.96, "duration": 7.04}, {"text": "The coid9 pandemic claimed the lives of", "start": 1128.799, "duration": 6.401}, {"text": "millions of people around the world.", "start": 1132.0, "duration": 5.919}, {"text": "But it also sent a message to the world", "start": 1135.2, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "for the global community to survive.", "start": 1137.919, "duration": 4.721}, {"text": "Mutual assistance, empathy and", "start": 1140.559, "duration": 6.201}, {"text": "cooperation are indispensable.", "start": 1142.64, "duration": 4.12}, {"text": "It is essential to ensure sustainable", "start": 1148.48, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "production of vaccines, therapeutics and", "start": 1151.76, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "diagnostic equipment in developing", "start": 1155.12, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "countries so that these are readily", "start": 1157.6, "duration": 6.079}, {"text": "accessible to all. Mr. president.", "start": 1159.6, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "A state can never become strong by", "start": 1163.679, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "keeping its citizens powerless", "start": 1166.32, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "through ensuring the political and", "start": 1169.919, "duration": 4.721}, {"text": "economic empowerment of the people. We", "start": 1171.84, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "want to build a prosperous,", "start": 1174.64, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "self-reliant, welfare oriented", "start": 1176.48, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "democratic state where everyone", "start": 1178.96, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "irrespective of political affiliation,", "start": 1181.44, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "religion or ethnicity can live with", "start": 1184.16, "duration": 5.759}, {"text": "security and peace and with equal", "start": 1186.96, "duration": 9.0}, {"text": "rights, honor and dignity. Mr. President", "start": 1189.919, "duration": 6.041}, {"text": "Bangladesh continues to make progress in", "start": 1198.4, "duration": 6.399}, {"text": "all areas including democracy, human", "start": 1201.28, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "rights, good governance, accountability,", "start": 1204.799, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "political stability and the investment", "start": 1207.6, "duration": 5.24}, {"text": "environment.", "start": 1209.84, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "The government is working to establish a", "start": 1213.36, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "safe and stable Bangladesh with a", "start": 1216.0, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "business and investment friendly", "start": 1218.64, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "environment. In today's democratic", "start": 1220.96, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "Bangladesh, we welcome partnership,", "start": 1223.6, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "innovation and both domestic and foreign", "start": 1225.84, "duration": 5.199}, {"text": "investment.", "start": 1228.72, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "We want to build a Bangladesh where", "start": 1231.039, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "young people can pursue their dreams", "start": 1234.32, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "without fear or hindrance.", "start": 1237.679, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "where women can lead their lives with", "start": 1240.88, "duration": 5.279}, {"text": "confidence.", "start": 1243.28, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "Where every child grows up with the", "start": 1246.159, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "opportunity to realize their full", "start": 1248.32, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "potential and above all where people are", "start": 1250.559, "duration": 7.281}, {"text": "assured of a safe and peaceful life.", "start": 1254.0, "duration": 6.799}, {"text": "That is why we say Bangladesh first,", "start": 1257.84, "duration": 7.079}, {"text": "Bangladesh for all.", "start": 1260.799, "duration": 4.12}, {"text": "I conclude my address by reaffirming", "start": 1266.64, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "Bangladesh's unwavering commitment to", "start": 1270.159, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "the values and principles of the United", "start": 1272.72, "duration": 5.839}, {"text": "Nations in order to build a peaceful", "start": 1274.96, "duration": 7.36}, {"text": "world. Mr. President, thank you. Allah", "start": 1278.559, "duration": 7.561}, {"text": "Bangladesh, zindabad.", "start": 1282.32, "duration": 3.8}, {"text": "On behalf of the assembly,", "start": 1292.0, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "I wish to thank Mr. Tarak Rahman, Prime", "start": 1294.48, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "Minister of the People's Republic of", "start": 1298.0, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "Bangladesh.", "start": 1300.24, "duration": 5.72}, {"text": "Thank you.", "start": 1302.72, "duration": 3.24}]